    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33280" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pābŭlātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		pabulor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>pasture.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 3, 16</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 7, 9 <i>fin.</i></span></i>— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, in milit. language, <i>a collecting of fodder</i>, <i>a foraging</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnes nostras pabulationes frumentationesque
					observabat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. G. 7, 16</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">1, 15</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">premi pabulatione,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. B.
					C. 1, 78</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pabulatione intercludi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. B.
					G. 7, 44</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Hirt. B. G. 8, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11</span></i>.</div>
